  abstract = {The Automotive Research Center is a U.S. Army Center of Excellence for the modeling and simulation of ground vehicles, led by the University of Michigan. We focus on basic scientific problems associated with ground vehicles, including autonomy, management of power and energy within vehicles, mobility and survivability of the complete vehicle system. Each year, we bring together members of the automotive research community from across academia, government and industry to share our latest research developments. It is an opportunity to discuss Army-relevant efforts, and to leverage and transfer our efforts to industry. See the full agenda here: https://arc.engin.umich.edu/events/annual-program-review/agenda/},
